<author id="281137">davido</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;I have to admit, I hate the idea of the trailing &lt;c&gt;::&lt;/c&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you're enumerating the ways to quote things in Perl, don't forget HERE docs:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;c&gt;
&lt;&lt;HERE              # Double quoted
&lt;&lt;"HERE"            # Double quoted, explicit.
&lt;&lt;'HERE'            # Single quoted, explicit.
&lt;&lt;\HERE             # Single quoted, uncommonly used.
&lt;&lt;`HERE`            # Same as qx or ``.
&lt;&lt;~HERE             # Double quoted, indented.
&lt;&lt;~"HERE"           # Double quoted, indented.
&lt;&lt;~'HERE'           # Single quoted, indented.
&lt;&lt;~\HERE            # Single quoted, indented, uncommonly used (I'll bet you could grep all of CPAN and not find this).
&lt;&lt;~`HERE`           # Same as qx / ``, indented.
&lt;/c&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Which made me think, too bad we don't have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;c&gt;
&lt;&lt;~/HERE/x           # Regexp object, indented, multi-line freeform (/x modifier).
&lt;/c&gt;


